id: pm-evidence-fragment-text-sdk
title: Resolve live fragment text through the public SDK
description: "pm-web PR 278 cannot render live fragments independently of historical retention through the published SDK. Expose a pure text-only entry to the existing exact resolver using the same strict text and descriptor schema as citation producers; no source I/O, state writes or duplicate JSON normalization."
type: Task
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[1]: "gh:unbraind/pm-evidence#19"
created_at: "2026-10-29T08:33:42.578Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-31T00:49:45.531Z"
assignee: codex-agent
claim_principal: codex-agent
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "Root SDK export resolves unchanged and changed file, heading and raw JSON spans independently of retained originals; large integer, exponent, escaped string and own prototype-key spellings remain exact; invalid inputs return typed safe remedies; 500 seeded sequences re-read native SDK state unchanged; npm and Bun packed consumers import the public export."
comments[11]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-29T08:33:59.877Z",codex-agent,"Adds resolveFragmentText(text, descriptor) as a pure public entry to the existing production resolveFragment implementation, with one strict request schema composed from producer text/descriptor schemas. No selector, JSON parser, source reader or native writer is duplicated. Focused source/SDK tests passed 9/9, including 500 seeded sequences, 2036 random source operations, six producer descriptors, older replays, whitespace/CRLF, exact raw JSON spellings, and native SDK read-back after every sequence in a Gitless tracker. Linked consumer work is pm-web-5sx6 / pm-web-cnhi and PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-web/pull/278."
  "2026-10-29T08:45:21.506Z",codex-agent,"The linked focused suite passed 9/9 via pm test --run --progress (500 sequences, 2036 operations, six selectors, native SDK read-back preserved). Typechecks, lint, zero duplication (80 sources) and docstrings (27 files / 127 declarations) pass. Mutation proof in a disposable copy: changing only resolveFragmentText to JSON parse/stringify normalization fails the 1e309 exact-exponent assertion (null instead of the raw span); the source checkout was untouched and the fixed boundary test passed again. Packed npm/npx and Bun/bunx/global acceptance now imports the public root export and asserts exact large-integer, exponent, escaped-string and prototype-key spans; its genuine packed journey is running. No new mutation/import/export/sync path was added."
  "2026-10-29T08:49:13.296Z",codex-agent,"Distribution decision: the web consumer must pin this SDK commit without a release or publish. Compiled JavaScript and declaration files are included explicitly in the commit so npm/Bun consumers that disable lifecycle scripts still receive the public entrypoint. These are deterministic text distribution files, not binary/cache artifacts. Existing build scripts and runtime dependency versions are unchanged. Full npm/Bun CI remains required; packed tests cover the root export in real installed consumers."
  "2026-10-29T08:58:52.714Z",codex-agent,"Genuine packed acceptance passed 2/2: npm/npx and native Bun/bunx, including global installs, existing portable bundle journeys and the new root-export exact-span probes. The API source and producer contracts are unchanged after those tests. Compiled JS, declaration and source-map text is now staged for commit-pinned consumers; no binary/cache files are included. PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-evidence/pull/19 is draft pending full npm/Bun CI. Claim released for independent verification; do not close this item."
  "2026-10-31T00:00:37.060Z",codex-agent,"Review round: fetched the complete PR review-thread connection (zero threads, no pagination); reviews API is empty. Latest CodeRabbit comment skips automatic review and contains no Outside diff range findings. Merged origin/main before changes. Issue #20 is valid: all compiled entrypoints are absent from Git while dist is ignored. General rule: every documented scripts-disabled install must contain the full runtime/declaration graph at the exact immutable dependency revision. Audit the entire dist inventory, packed and commit-pinned npm/Bun journeys, root SDK exports and host CLI commands in non-git trackers; preserve source exactness and unchanged thresholds."
  "2026-10-31T00:01:13.075Z",codex-agent,"Correction after exact tree inspection: issue #20 names 00d770c; the fetched PR head dddf9e0 already tracks 56 dist entries (added in the prior round), despite the remaining ignore rule. The valid unresolved class is missing immutable git-consumer proof and source/artifact drift enforcement. The merge advances source VERSION from 2026.10.28 to 2026.10.30 without rebuilding those artifacts. Add a gate comparing every committed runtime/declaration/map file against a pristine compiler output before builds can mask drift, plus real scripts-disabled tarball/git installs. Local pm health currently reports only extension_host_pm_cli_version_skew for the ignored pm-github install; history integrity is clean and no merge receipt reconciliation was requested."
  "2026-10-31T00:03:28.894Z",codex-agent,"Focused red proof before rebuild: node --test --test-concurrency=1 test/distribution.acceptance.ts returned 1/2 pass, 1/2 fail. HEAD dist/index.js differs from pristine source build (compiled extension version 2026.10.28 vs source 2026.10.30). The independent graph oracle passed with 168 missing/stale/extra mutations refused across all 56 emitted paths. Release ordering now runs dist:check before any build can hide this condition; remove the dist ignore rule to expose future generated files. Added exact HEAD local Git mirror installs to every existing npm/Bun CLI, global, SDK, JSON and TOON journey, checking every installed byte and declaration resolution."
  "2026-10-31T00:09:45.956Z",codex-agent,"Focused git/npm reached successful scripts-disabled installation, matching all 56 committed bytes and CLI journeys, then the new declaration compiler exposed a fixture omission: explicitly select --types node for TypeScript 7. The host Bun 1.3.5 rejects git+file pinned SHAs before package code; the official Bun 1.4 notes document this exact upstream fix (https://bun.sh/blog/bun-v1.4). Retain the real git matrix and use an isolated current Bun binary for verification, without upgrading the shared host. Added explicit manifest main/types/nested exports/bin graph assertions so a working modern conditional export cannot conceal another broken advertised entrypoint."
  "2026-10-31T00:12:10.087Z",codex-agent,"Hostile review completed across the whole PR diff and every public distribution entrypoint. General artifact rule covers all 56 emitted runtime/declaration/map paths and every manifest main/types/exports/bin target, including declarations hidden by conditional exports; the oracle rejects 168 file mutations plus four nested entrypoint mutations. Source resolver delegates to the existing exact selector implementation, preserves legacy records and requires no Git/I/O. Existing 500-sequence producer/state property test passes 9/9 focused cases. Current isolated Bun 1.4.4 successfully installed the exact Git commit with scripts disabled and all 56 bytes match; retain full journey and revert checks before final gates."
  "2026-10-31T00:16:15.375Z",codex-agent,"Revert proof recorded explicitly (linked test-result tracking is disabled): PATH selecting isolated Bun 1.4.4, pm test pm-evidence-fragment-text-sdk --run --only-last --progress --timeout 1800 ran npm run test:dist:revert, passed 2/2 in disposable clones. With only dist removed and that mutant committed, pristine graph gate failed exactly 1/2 and all four real npm/Bun packed/git scripts-disabled consumers failed 4/4 on absent compiled directories. Every failure must match the artifact refusal, excluding transport/setup errors. With only dist/index.js runtime version changed and committed, graph gate failed exactly 1/2 on compiled/source byte drift. The fixed source tree is untouched; npm run dist:check passed 2/2 afterward. Fresh independent clone with real npm ci and strict pm health passed (no installed-extension version skew; no history drift). Full npm/Bun release gates next at unchanged 100/100/100/100 and zero duplication."
  "2026-10-31T00:49:37.624Z",codex-agent,"Additional same-class integration found by hostile review: release.yml rebuilt new versioned artifacts, ran release:check, and only then committed them. Immutable Git artifact validation correctly refuses that old HEAD. Move the existing local Commit release files step before Run release checks; keep artifact packing/upload and every remote publication after successful validation, with unchanged approval/permissions. Regression node --test --test-concurrency=1 test/release-distribution.test.ts passed 1/1: execute the actual version/build and local-commit scripts in disposable clones; the prepared commit passes dist:check 2/2, and restoring only the former check-before-commit ordering makes parity fail 1/2 on HEAD dist/index.js. No publishing or tag step is executed. The provisional npm gate began before this added case; repeat the full final-head npm gate after the final Bun gate so both cover the integration regression. Official step execution reference: https://docs.github.com/en/actions/reference/workflows-and-actions/workflow-syntax#jobsjob_idsteps"
